# What this repository leaves out. Rewritten on 2026-10-17 from a 205-line Python project template:
# its broad rules (`lib/`, `dist/`, a bare `opend/`) swallowed real source three times and needed
# negations to undo. Only rules for things this repo actually produces are kept, so there is nothing
# left to negate.

# secrets and live state, never committed (CLAUDE.md)
.env
data/

# dependencies and environments
node_modules/
.venv/

# Python caches, and what `uv build` would write. Inside the uv workspace (ADR 0021) a build of either
# member lands in the ROOT's dist/, not the member's; python/dist/ is where it lands from a copy of the
# library on its own. Both anchored, for the reason /opend/ is below.
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
/dist/
python/dist/

# the frontend bundle IS committed (ADR 0005), which is why no dist/ rule above is a bare `dist/`

# playwright writes test traces and screenshots beside the tests it runs
frontend/src/__browser__/__screenshots__/
frontend/test-results/

# the OpenD install, if unpacked here. Anchored: a bare `opend/` matches at ANY depth, and from
# 2026-10-02 to 2026-10-16 it silently left backend/src/opend/ — the API's websocket client — out of
# every clone while the working tree that runs still had it.
/opend/

# notebooks written against the package stay local
*.ipynb
.ipynb_checkpoints/

# OS and editor noise
.DS_Store
*.log
